# Container-local PAM stack for sudo in the netadmin machine.
# No pam_nologin: login-shell.target never runs systemd-user-sessions,
# so /run/nologin persists for the machine's whole life. sudo is the
# only PAM consumer here, and authorization stays in the sudoers file.
# The account phase gates on the role account name instead of pam_unix:
# pam_unix needs the setuid unix_chkpwd helper, which cannot load
# libcrypt in this minimal machine (proven live across *, empty, and
# valid-hash shadow states), so pam_unix can never succeed here. The
# gate mirrors the sudoers invoker restriction (defense in depth).
auth     sufficient pam_unix.so
auth     required   pam_deny.so
account  requisite  pam_succeed_if.so user = netadmin
password sufficient pam_unix.so sha512 shadow try_first_pass use_authtok
password required   pam_deny.so
session  required   pam_unix.so
